    "result_text": "Full suite green: **280 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors. BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation. When creating an owner, it's set to `true` if another owner already had the same address and city at that moment, otherwise `false` \u2014 creation is always allowed.\n\nBecause the acceptance test reads the flag back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (and asserts the *first* owner at an address stays `false` even after a second one joins), the value is a **snapshot persisted at creation time**, mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` pattern rather than being recomputed on read.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates into `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it by name).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 new `Boolean sharesHousehold` field (`shares_household` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`AssignSharesHousehold.java`** (new function) \u2014 checks existing owners for a matching address + city and sets the flag. Runs before the new owner is saved, so it never matches itself.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in after `assignNamesakeCount`, before `save`, under the same `transaction` governance. Placed after `normalizeCity` so it compares against the canonical city spelling.\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the `shares_household` column; updated the hsqldb seed `data.sql` positional inserts with the extra value (the active test profile). h2/postgres use column-list inserts (unaffected); mysql's seed was already positionally out of sync pre-existing and is unused by tests.",
